<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<LVClass LVVersion="13008000">
	<Property Name="NI.Lib.DefaultMenu" Type="Str">BaseResponder.mnu</Property>
	<Property Name="NI.Lib.Description" Type="Str">The Responder class emits responses from a driver to the owning application. Responses are a type-def with the following members:
Name: The name of the Responder, so that the owning application can identify the sender
Driver Status: Enum with driver states. If it is "Normal" the contained response is a message from the remote destination the driver communicates with
Variant: The data in the response, application specific
Type: A number to identify what data is contained in the variant. Application specific .

Overide the BaseResponder class with your own implementation to create responders that can use whatever means you want to send responses to the application, such as queues, events, etc
</Property>
